=F0=9F=93=96 Estimated read time: 4 minutes =F0=9F=91=8B Hi Wellness IQ Crew!=
 Over the past few weeks, we have been talking about smarter supplement choic=
es.=C2=A0We talked about=C2=A0creatine=C2=A0for muscle, energy, and healthy a=
ging.=C2=A0We talked about=C2=A0magnesium=C2=A0and why the form matters.=C2=
=A0Then we talked about=C2=A0electrolytes=C2=A0and how hydration is not alway=
s as simple as drinking more water.=C2=A0And I have to tell you,=C2=A0I loved=
 hearing from so many of you. Some of you checked your bottles and realized y=
ou were already making good choices.=C2=A0Others said the articles helped you=
 finally understand what to look for. Some of you created Fullscript accounts=
. And yes, a few of you have started choosing better options through my dispe=
nsary.=C2=A0That is exactly the point.=C2=A0Not more supplements just for the=
 sake of taking more supplements. Smarter choices. Better quality. Less guess=
ing. More Wellness IQ. So this week, let=E2=80=99s build on that with a quest=
ion I hear all the time in the summer:=C2=A0Why am I so tired? =F0=9F=91=89=
=C2=A0Let=E2=80=99s Raise Your Wellness IQ Summer fatigue can be real. Heat, =
sweat, poor sleep, travel, alcohol, inconsistent meals, too little protein, b=
lood sugar swings, dehydration, and low mineral intake can all leave you feel=
ing more drained than usual. Sometimes the answer is not one thing. It is the=
 combination. =E2=98=80=EF=B8=8F Heat Takes Energy When it is hot outside, yo=
ur body has to work harder to stay cool.=C2=A0That can leave you feeling more=
 tired, especially if you are outside for long periods of time, walking, exer=
cising, gardening, sitting at outdoor events, traveling, or running around wi=
th kids and grandkids.=C2=A0You may not think of heat as a stressor, but your=
 body does.=C2=A0Heat can affect your energy, mood, appetite, sleep, hydratio=
n, and recovery.=C2=A0That does not mean something is =E2=80=9Cwrong=E2=80=9D=
 with you.=C2=A0It may simply mean your body is working harder than you reali=
ze. =F0=9F=92=A7 Hydration Is Part of the Energy Story Water matters . . . a=
=C2=A0lot! But when you sweat, you lose more than water. You also lose electr=
olytes, especially sodium. If you are drinking water but still feeling wiped =
out after heat, sweat, travel, workouts, alcohol, or long days outside,=C2=A0=
it may be worth thinking about electrolyte support. Not every day.=C2=A0Not a=
ll day long.=C2=A0And not because electrolytes are trendy. Because sometimes =
your body needs more than plain water to feel replenished. =F0=9F=91=89=C2=A0=
See My Favorite Clean Electrolyte Options Here:=C2=A0=C2=A0FULLSCRIPT LINK =
=F0=9F=98=B4 Sleep Can Get Messy in the Summer Longer days, later nights, tra=
vel, heat, alcohol, inconsistent routines, and more screen time can all affec=
t sleep. And poor sleep can make everything feel harder the next day. You may=
 crave more sugar, rely on more caffeine, feel less motivated to exercise, or=
 feel like you are dragging even if you technically got enough hours in bed. =
This is one reason I talk so often about=C2=A0magnesium glycinate. Magnesium =
is not a magic sleep pill, but it is often chosen for relaxation, stress supp=
ort, muscle relaxation, and gentle daily magnesium support. If you missed the=
 magnesium article, this is a good time to check your bottle.=C2=A0The form m=
atters. =F0=9F=91=89=C2=A0See My Favorite Magnesium Glycinate Options Here:=
=C2=A0FULLSCRIPT LINK =F0=9F=8D=BD=EF=B8=8F Blood Sugar Swings Can Feel Like =
Fatigue Summer schedules can throw off eating patterns. Maybe breakfast gets =
skipped. Maybe lunch is lighter than usual. Maybe dinner is later. Maybe ther=
e are more chips, cocktails, ice cream, desserts, barbecues, and snacky meals=
. No judgment.=C2=A0That is summer. But big gaps between meals, too little pr=
otein, too much sugar, or too many refined carbs can lead to blood sugar ups =
and downs.=C2=A0And those dips can feel like: =F0=9F=8C=BF fatigue =F0=9F=8C=
=BF brain fog =F0=9F=8C=BF irritability =F0=9F=8C=BF cravings =F0=9F=8C=BF sh=
akiness =F0=9F=8C=BF afternoon crashes =F0=9F=8C=BF needing more caffeine One=
 simple place to start: Build meals and snacks around protein, fiber, healthy=
 fats, and color. Food first . . .=C2=A0Always. But sometimes, having a few s=
mart supports on hand makes it easier to stay consistent. =F0=9F=92=AA Protei=
n, Muscles, and Minerals Matter Too If you are not getting enough protein, yo=
u may feel it. Protein helps support muscle, blood sugar balance, recovery, i=
mmune function, and healthy aging. And as we age, protein becomes even more i=
mportant. This is not about bodybuilding. It is about staying strong, steady,=
 energized, and resilient. Minerals=C2=A0matter too. Magnesium and electrolyt=
es help support fluid balance, muscle function, nerve signaling, energy produ=
ction, relaxation, and healthy stress response. When you sweat more, eat inco=
nsistently, drink more alcohol, travel, or rely on convenience foods, mineral=
 intake and balance can suffer. This does not mean everyone needs a pile of s=
upplements. It means minerals and protein are worth paying attention to. =F0=
=9F=91=89 Quick Wellness IQ Check If you have been feeling unusually tired th=
is summer, ask yourself: =F0=9F=8C=BF Am I drinking enough water? =F0=9F=8C=
=BF Am I sweating more than usual? =F0=9F=8C=BF Do I need electrolytes someti=
mes? =F0=9F=8C=BF Am I sleeping well? =F0=9F=8C=BF Am I getting enough protei=
n? =F0=9F=8C=BF Am I skipping meals or grazing on snacks? =F0=9F=8C=BF Am I d=
rinking more alcohol than usual? =F0=9F=8C=BF Am I relying on caffeine to pus=
h through? =F0=9F=8C=BF Am I choosing supplements thoughtfully, or just guess=
ing? That last question matters. Because the supplement aisle can be overwhel=
ming. And the internet can be even worse. That is why I am putting more focus=
 on helping you make better supplement choices, one topic at a time. =F0=9F=
=92=8A Where My Fullscript Dispensary Comes In My goal is not to convince you=
 to take every supplement. My goal is to help you make smarter choices when a=
 supplement makes sense. Fullscript is my trusted professional supplement dis=
pensary, used by health practitioners to recommend carefully vetted, high qua=
lity products from brands preferred by clinicians. Instead of guessing online=
, comparing hundreds of products, or grabbing whatever looks good on a shelf,=
 I am creating simple, practical Fullscript lists around the topics we are di=
scussing. This week, I created a short list of my favorite summer energy supp=
ort options. The goal is simple: =F0=9F=8C=BF better quality =F0=9F=8C=BF tru=
sted brands =F0=9F=8C=BF less confusion =F0=9F=8C=BF fewer impulse buys =F0=
=9F=8C=BF smarter support for real-life wellness Depending on your needs, tha=
t may include options for hydration, electrolytes, magnesium, protein, or ene=
rgy metabolism support. =F0=9F=91=89=C2=A0See My Favorite Summer Energy Suppo=
rt Options Here:=C2=A0FULLSCRIPT LINK Please bookmark this link. You always s=
ave 15%, or 20% with auto ship, and you are welcome to share it with family a=
nd friends. =E2=9C=85 A Smart Safety Note Fatigue can have many causes. Heat,=
 hydration, sleep, stress, blood sugar, nutrition, hormones, medications, thy=
roid function, anemia, infection, and other health concerns can all play a ro=
le. If your fatigue is new, severe, persistent, unusual for you, or comes wit=
h symptoms like dizziness, shortness of breath, chest pain, fainting, rapid h=
eartbeat, confusion, weakness, or unexplained weight loss, please check with =
your healthcare provider. Supplements can be helpful tools, but they are not =
a substitute for appropriate medical care. =F0=9F=92=A1 Final Thought Summer =
is supposed to feel fun. But heat, sweat, travel, late nights, alcohol, disru=
pted routines, and inconsistent meals can all catch up with you. If you are f=
eeling more tired than usual, do not just push harder. Pause and ask better q=
uestions. Am I hydrated? Am I sleeping? Am I eating enough protein? Am I keep=
ing blood sugar steady? Am I replenishing minerals when it makes sense? Am I =
choosing better quality supplements, or am I just guessing? That is Wellness =
IQ. See you next time. And as always, be cool to your future self. =F0=9F=98=
=8E Wishing you wellness =F0=9F=8C=BA Gloria Gloria Treister HHP, Board Certi=
fied Holistic Health Practitioner, Advanced Physical Fitness Specialist, EMCC=
 Certified Executive and Business Coach ,Author:=C2=A0Wellness 101: Simple St=
eps to Good Health=C2=A0 Follow Me On LinkedIn
